comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-03T20:11:29.225Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: strict all-status full-body corpus 2867/2867 with complete receipt and zero omissions/unreadables. Examined all matching settings/snapshot/cursor/platform titles and full shipped semantic-preview owner pm-gh1370; pm-2zjs0g is expressly rate measurement rather than individual repairs and stays open/unclaimed. No existing leaf owns these new persistent-path classification and canonical-injection causes. Original nightly run 37114037678 remains failing evidence; Ubuntu Node22 repair is already shipped separately under pm-5iwfkj."
  "2026-10-03T20:12:46.090Z","harness:codex","Test-audit rationale: retain actual filesystem state transitions and propagation of structural/permission/link failures; normalize the chosen path spelling so injection executes rather than weakening expected results. Extend the existing snapshot fault table with Windows ENOENT-below-file and nested missing-ancestor cases; the production classifier must distinguish these without treating a persistent error as a retryable race. Search cursor fingerprint should bind its documented resolved scope consistently."
  "2026-10-03T20:26:46.648Z","harness:codex","TDD negative controls on the unchanged production tree: 6 expected failures and 58 passes. The Windows ENOENT boundary now reproduces on Linux by translating only the actual lstat ENOTDIR syscall failure below a real regular file. Native assertions are retained. Search scopes now normalize through the shared SDK fingerprint. Canonical settings race injection targets fs.realpath output; native macOS and Windows regression checks cover these files before merge."
  "2026-10-03T20:57:05.089Z","harness:codex","Platform classification now checks every ancestor including the filesystem root: retry only when the nearest existing ancestor is a directory; preserve the original native error for regular-file ancestors, dangling entries, denied lookup, missing provenance, and an unavailable root. Boundary tests perform real lstat checks and emulate only native error outcomes, retaining actual snapshot reads/writes. A deterministic source-scope test binds relative and absolute search paths to one cursor identity. The interrupted overloaded local validation was not counted as a pass; dedicated low-worker full coverage and hosted gates remain mandatory."
  "2026-10-03T21:23:47.867Z","harness:codex","Draft gates correctly refused the first head: the new SDK spec exceeded the existing 120-file directory cap and the recorded recurrence edge formed a new unregistered component. Moved the spec into the established SDK transactions suite without changing the cap or assertions, migrated its live PM file/test links, and registered the semantic preview scope/path family with actual native PR checks, a selecting negative control, and historical gh1370 evidence. No waiver or gate relaxation was used. The local full run was interrupted rather than counted as green; exact all-source coverage remains required on the final hosted head."
  "2026-10-03T21:47:51.234Z","harness:codex","Required CI regression repair: the initial PR head passed the focused macOS and Windows portability jobs, but static/full-suite gates correctly rejected a 121-entry flat SDK test directory and an unregistered recurrence component. The new settings spec now lives in the existing transactions domain without raising the 120-entry cap. The recorded recurs_from lineage has a concrete policy family bound to mandatory static, coverage, Windows and macOS jobs. CI assertions now verify every artifact-consuming test step reuses its validated build instead of relying on a brittle total step count, with platform requirements in a separate complexity-bounded test. Latest organization/policy run: 31 tests across 3 files pass; focused linked runs pass. Previous failed/interrupted runs remain recorded and are not counted as certification."
  "2026-10-03T21:54:58.113Z","harness:codex","Live release/observability boundary check: today has one successful native scheduled Auto Release (37109948652), GitHub release and public npm both expose immutable 2026.10.3. Automatic workflow serializes attempts and reuses an existing exact-day tag before preparation; it does not create another automatic same-day version. These branch repairs remain separate from that earlier publication. Recent Sentry gate observed zero critical/high blockers, telemetry finish error rate 1.42 percent and zero missing error-code rows, and a real queue flush drained one event successfully. No trace rows were returned, so complete end-to-end action/trace coverage is not certified."
  "2026-10-03T22:05:47.371Z","harness:codex","Hosted head 50f7ff9ee failure analysis: static tracker-context quality found this new owner missing risk/confidence/estimate/expected behavior. Those planning fields are now supplied through pm. Coverage shard 4 and native Windows failed the existing gate-registry test because it copied families[0] and asserted the boundary-format family ID after a new family was inserted. The fixture now selects its stable ID explicitly and uses the public policy type, preserving the exact matrix-rename refusal assertion. This is a fixture-order dependency, not a weakened production registry check."
  "2026-10-03T22:34:18.309Z","harness:codex","Round-two gate remediation: native portability cases passed, but the newly registered recurrence family exposed an existing gate-registry test that selected the first family while asserting a different fixed ID. The fixture now selects boundary-format-drift by ID and retains the stale matrix-check refusal assertion. Hosted tracker-context quality also required risk, confidence, estimate and expected-result metadata; these are now supplied through pm. The linked CI/recurrence verification command was replaced, not duplicated, to include the gate-registry regression. Nightly and aggregate coverage failures from that head are retained as failures, pending a fresh complete run."
  "2026-10-03T22:40:35.791Z","harness:codex","Production/source verification at ce81a2fe9: both linked commands passed, with 211 runtime tests and 33 workflow/recurrence tests. The complete native nightly and PR checks are running on the repaired source. GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning and secret-scanning live inventories each contain zero open alerts; the local tracked-file secret scanner passes. Sentry/telemetry live gate passes for the last day: no critical/high issue and no missing error-code telemetry rows; finish error rate 1.42 percent is within its 6 percent guardrail. This is bounded production observation, not proof of every individual action or complete tracing. Reviewer availability limits (CodeRabbit/cubic/Sourcery quota receipts) are retained independently of approval, and Greptile P1 preservation remediation is linked to the paired SDK owner."
  "2026-10-03T22:54:26.473Z","harness:codex","Exact graph remediation: a full prose-reference comparison against the initial complete corpus identified only two new missing pairs: this owner cites the already closed supported-Node22 snapshot repair, and the SDK owner cites the canonical semantic-docstring debt. Added a verifies relationship to the existing Node22 owner and a discovered_from relationship from the documentation owner to the current SDK observations. The graph-composition gate now passes with 1236 prose gaps, retaining its original ceiling; semantic/verification edges increased with evidence, and no synthetic ancestry or historical knowledge was invented."
  "2026-10-03T23:00:08.742Z","harness:codex","Local full static attempt at the earlier source head reached SDK import-cost benchmarking after dependency, docstring, export, ESLint, duplicate, workflow, generated-contract, static-assurance, package, grammar, refusal, token and tracker stages passed. The local runtime/host measured imports above unchanged budgets (for example governance median 494ms versus 327ms, runtime 791ms versus 452ms), so this run is a failure and is not counted as a full pass. The same exact source head passed hosted SDK-entrypoint and transport budgets before its graph refusal. Preserve both results; final hosted static including performance, graph, record integrity and mutation remains mandatory on the corrected head. No baseline or time ceiling is raised."
  "2026-10-03T23:23:34.876Z","harness:codex","Final source-head PR checks: all mandatory checks passed except Packed first run (Ubuntu Node22.18.0), whose real detached-telemetry collector reached its unchanged 90-second AbortSignal deadline awaiting command_finish. The other five packed first-run profiles, dedicated Node22 telemetry check, full exact coverage/static/typecheck/compat/smokes/analyzers and complete native nightly all passed. The failed log is retained; the timeout does not establish a production cause. Rerun only that failed job once against identical source and existing deadlines, preserving the initial failure rather than weakening the collector or acceptance gate. If it repeats, investigate the telemetry producer/collector boundary before closure."
  "2026-10-03T23:27:33.963Z","harness:codex","Final implementation proof: all seven jobs of native nightly 37160329211 pass on 6bdb71d86, including Ubuntu22/24/25, macOS24, both Windows24 shards and full quality. Exact all-source coverage is 100 in all four categories (66577 statements, 50934 branches, 13751 functions, 63475 lines; all covered). Every required PR check is now green after the isolated Node22.18 first-run retry passed with unchanged source and collector deadlines; its initial detached-telemetry timeout remains recorded as a failure. The paired owner-linked commands pass 211 runtime plus 33 gate-policy tests. Hosted static/performance/graph/history/mutation and analyzer provenance pass; local import-cost budget refusal remains a separate limitation, not a local full-pass claim. No security alert is open, and bounded recent Sentry/telemetry checks pass. Both accepted review findings are fixed; unavailable Sourcery/cubic reviews remain explicit."
